{"GoogleCalendarService.fetchAvailabilityAndSetCache calls updateManyByCredentialId with an empty update object, so no fields change and SelectedCalendar.updatedAt will not be bumped as the comment claims, causing downstream logic/UI that relies on updatedAt to show stale values": 0.9336450099945068, "The cache timestamp is formatted using new Intl.DateTimeFormat with a hardcoded 'en-US' locale instead of using the user's actual locale from useLocale, breaking internationalization": 0.9080249667167664, "The deleteCacheHandler enforces userId: user.id for authorization, completely blocking users from deleting the cache of team credentials since team credentials have userId: null and teamId populated instead": 0.9127076268196106, "deleteCacheHandler throws a plain Error when the credential is missing or not owned by the user, which tRPC will surface as an INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR instead of a NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN, breaking API semantics and making monitoring treat expected access failures as server faults": 0.8116170763969421}